<title>USA: Boyd Bros Q4 shr $0.07 vs $0.09.</title>
<headline>Boyd Bros Q4 shr $0.07 vs $0.09.</headline>
<dateline>CLAYTON 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr		 $0.07		    $0.09</p>
<p> Net		 247			351</p>
<p> Oper revs	 16,715		   15,411</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  3,700		    3,823</p>
<p>	  12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr		 0.22		     0.56</p>
<p> Net		 827			2,124</p>
<p> Oper revs	 65,523		   61,865</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  3,726		    3,823</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Full company name is Boyd Brothers Transportation Inc.</p>
<p>1995 Q4 earnings benefited from $150,000, or $0.04 per share, gains on sale of equipment and a positive adjustment to the company's environmental reserve that did no recur in 1996.</p>
<p>1996 net includes $0.13 a share gain on the sale of equipment.</p>
<p>1995 net includes $0.11 a share gain from the same sale as well as a $0.05 a share gain from positive adjustment to environmental reserve.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
